{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.HeliumFourBodyCluster","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HeliumFourBodyCluster","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.lift_is_coefficient_ratio_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.lift_is_coefficient_ratio_order","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L166-L176","doc":"**Order-invariance of a level lift, any Milnor order.**  For two deficits at\nthe SAME order `m`, `h^m·κ₁ h` and `h^m·κ₂ h` (`h ≠ 0`, `κ₂ h ≠ 0`), the lift\nratio is `κ₁ h / κ₂ h` — the shared `h^m` cancels.  A width-cable level lift is a\npure coefficient rescale and can NEVER change the Milnor order; the A=4 cabling\npreserves `O(h⁶)` exactly as the A=3 cabling preserved `O(h⁴)` (#4364). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Order_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Order_eq","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L163-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Order","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L158-L161","doc":"The A=4 Brunnian Milnor order is `6` (`= 2·(4−1)`), one Milnor step above the\nBorromean's `4`.  (Recorded as the derived exponent the companion probe measures;\n`O(h⁶)` vs the A=3 `O(h⁴)`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnianDeficitOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnianDeficitOrder","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L151-L156","doc":"A Brunnian-order-suppressed level deficit at Milnor order `m`:\n`D(h) = h^m · κ h`.  For an `n`-component Brunnian link the leading order is\n`m = 2(n − 1)` (every proper sub-link trivial kills all lower orders): the\nBorromean `n = 3` gives `m = 4` (#4364), the 4-component `n = 4` gives `m = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.sign_swap_a3_a4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.sign_swap_a3_a4","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L129-L147","doc":"**(CAPSTONE) The A=3 → A=4 sign SWAP.**  Read with #4360 (Brunnian deficit\n`≥ 0`) and #4354 (multiplicative cluster `≤ 0`):\n\n* `μ₃ > 0` lies on the *positive* side — compatible with the Brunnian deficit\n  (`c₃ ≥ 0`), incompatible with the multiplicative cluster (`≤ 0`);\n* `μ₄ < 0` lies on the *negative* side — incompatible with the Brunnian deficit\n  (`c₄ ≥ 0`, proved here), consistent with the multiplicative cluster (`≤ 0`).\n\nSo no single sign mechanism reproduces both isotopes: the Brunnian (binding)\noperator selects A=3, the multiplicative (saturation) operator selects A=4.  The\nBorromean-lift recipe does not carry the sign across the isotope step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mu4_ne_brunnian4Cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mu4_ne_brunnian4Cluster","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L115-L127","doc":"**(WALL, sign, scope-(b) conditional on `τ ≤ 1`)  The derived A=4 residual\n`μ₄ < 0` is unreachable by the Borromean-deficit binding recipe.**  If the\n4-component Brunnian level deficit is non-negative (`τ_L₄(h) ≤ 1`, the #4360\ninvariant), its cluster `c₄ = E₀·(1 − τ_L₄) ≥ 0`; but `μ₄ < 0`, so\n`μ₄ ≠ c₄`.  The same 0-fit recipe that supplied the A=3 `μ₃ > 0` sign gives the\nWRONG sign at A=4.  (Mirror of `Mu4RhoFCluster.mu3_ne_pairwise_3body_cluster`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Cluster_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Cluster_pos","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**The Brunnian binding cluster is strictly positive** in the physical regime\n(`E₀ > 0`, `τ h < 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Cluster_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Cluster_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L96-L104","doc":"**The Brunnian binding cluster is non-negative** whenever the level trace lies\nat or below the unlink (`τ h ≤ 1`) and the energy scale is non-negative — exactly\nthe #4360 shape `c₃ = E₀·(1 − τ_Borr) ≥ 0`, transported to A=4.  This is the\n*binding* half-line: a deficit against the unlink is a positive binding\ncontribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brunnian4Cluster","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L88-L94","doc":"The 4-body Brunnian **binding cluster** at level `τ`, realized the SAME way as\nthe A=3 Borromean cluster (#4360): the energy-scaled deficit of the link trace\nagainst the unlink, `c₄ = E₀·(1 − τ_L₄(h))`.  (\"Brunnian\": every proper sub-link\nis trivial, so the pairwise content vanishes and the whole is the irreducible\n4-body cluster.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.tauLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.tauLevel","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L83-L86","doc":"A level Markov trace as a function of `h = q − q⁻¹`, normalized so the\n`k`-component unlink is `τ(0) = 1` (writhe-0 trivial eigenvalue).  This is the\ngeneric shape #4360 used for the Borromean `H₃` trace `τ_Borr`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mu4Residual_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mu4Residual_neg","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L74-L79","doc":"**The derived A=4 residual is NEGATIVE.**  Unlike the positive 3-body moment\n`μ₃ = +0.4708`, the 4-body α-cluster residual `μ₄ = −4.591 < 0` — the closed\n`[1⁴]` SU(4) supermultiplet *saturation* signature (`μ₄ = s₄ − g₄`, the graded\nreference's `g₄ = +8.37` over-subtracts).  Forward, 0-fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mu4Residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mu4Residual","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HeliumFourBodyCluster.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The A=4 4-body simplex residual coefficient, from the exact 0-parameter\nback-substitution `μ₄ = M(4) − 6·μ₂ − 4·μ₃` on the derived coordination counts,\nevaluated at the canonical `q₀` (`deltalambda_kappa_interface_residual_simplex_probe.py`).\nRecorded as the derived numeric value; the sign — not the digits — is load-bearing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}